Input: {"question": "What year did the Battle of Ramla take place?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d00", "start": 0, "end": 45, "text": "place of Bohemond of Antioch, for assistance."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d00", "start": 46, "end": 188, "text": "Jaffa did not immediately capitulate, and when Baldwin returned victorious the following day the remaining Egyptian forces quickly scattered.."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d00", "start": 189, "end": 351, "text": "Ascalon remained in Fatimid hands, however, and a miscalculation would prove very costly to Baldwin when the two sides once again met at Ramla the following year."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d00", "start": 352, "end": 455, "text": "Egyptian armies of the period relied on masses of Sudanese bowmen supported by Arab and Berber cavalry."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d00", "start": 456, "end": 634, "text": "Since the archers were on foot and the horsemen awaited attack with lance and sword, an Egyptian army provided exactly the sort of immobile target that the Frankish heavy cavalry"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01", "start": 0, "end": 158, "text": "Battle of Ramla (1105) The third Battle of Ramla (or Ramleh) took place on 27 August 1105 between the Crusader Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Fatimids of Egypt."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01", "start": 159, "end": 286, "text": "The town of Ramla lay on the road from Jerusalem to Ascalon, the latter of which was the largest Fatimid fortress in Palestine."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01", "start": 287, "end": 430, "text": "From Ascalon the Fatimid vizier, Al-Afdal Shahanshah, launched almost annual attacks into the newly founded Crusader kingdom from 1099 to 1107."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01", "start": 431, "end": 542, "text": "Of the three battles the Crusaders fought at Ramla early in the twelfth century, the third was the most bloody."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01", "start": 543, "end": 589, "text": "Egyptian armies of the period relied on masses"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02", "start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "Fatimid fortress in Palestine ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02", "start": 32, "end": 178, "text": "From Ascalon the Fatimid vizier , Al-Afdal Shahanshah , launched almost annual attacks into the newly founded Crusader kingdom from 1099 to 1107 ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02", "start": 179, "end": 292, "text": "Of the three battles the Crusaders fought at Ramla early in the twelfth century , the third was the most bloody ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02", "start": 293, "end": 337, "text": "Quick Facts Third Battle of Ramla , Date ..."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02", "start": 338, "end": 616, "text": "Third Battle of Ramla Part of the Crusades Date 27 August 1105 Location Ramla 31°55′29.26″N 34°52′21.75″E Result Crusader victory Belligerents Kingdom of Jerusalem Fatimid Caliphate Burid dynasty Commanders and leaders Baldwin I of Jerusalem Sama ' al-Mulk Husayn General Sabawa"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d03", "start": 0, "end": 158, "text": "flee and escaped the tower under the cover of night with just his scribe and a single knight, Hugh of Brulis, who is never mentioned in any source afterwards."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d03", "start": 159, "end": 320, "text": "Baldwin spent the next two days evading Fatimid search parties until he arrived exhausted, starved and parched in the reasonably safe haven of Arsuf on May 19th."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d03", "start": 321, "end": 511, "text": "The situation of the remaining knights in Ramla deteriorated when Fatimid forces stormed the town on the morning after Baldwin's escape, with only the tower remaining under Crusader control."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d03", "start": 512, "end": 608, "text": "The Fatimids ruthlessly attacked the tower, undermining walls and setting fires to smoke out the"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d04", "start": 0, "end": 129, "text": "as the more fantastical exaggerations of some medieval chroniclers , but it was almost always larger than the armies it opposed ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d04", "start": 130, "end": 236, "text": "The Unexpected Enemy In May 1102 a huge Egyptian army poured out of Ascalon and onto the plain of Sharon ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d04", "start": 237, "end": 275, "text": "The invasion was a complete surprise ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d04", "start": 276, "end": 355, "text": "Advanced elements attacked Ramla and tried to flush out the Frankish garrison ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d04", "start": 356, "end": 493, "text": "The local bishop , Robert of Rouen , took the opportunity to send word to King Baldwin at Jaffa that Egyptian troops were close at hand ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d04", "start": 494, "end": 532, "text": "As far as we know , this was the first"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d05", "start": 0, "end": 567, "text": "Battle100953559 yago : Campaign100798245 yago : Conflict100958896 yago : Event100029378 yago : GroupAction101080366 yago : MilitaryAction100952963 yago : PsychologicalFeature100023100 yago : Work100575741 yago : YagoPermanentlyLocatedEntity dbo : Event dbo : MilitaryConflict yago : Undertaking100795720 yago : Venture100797878 yago : Wikicat12th-centuryCrusades umbel-rc : ConflictEvent umbel-rc : Event rdfs : comment La batalla de Ramla del 1102 fou la segona batalla entre l'exèrcit croat i l'exèrcit musulmà del Califat fatimita d'Egipte en la rodalia de Ramla ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d05", "start": 568, "end": 708, "text": "El resultat fou una terrible derrota dels croats , que només salvaren el reialme quan les tropes egípcies es desplaçaren a Jaffa i gràcies a"}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "1105", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01:c0", "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "1102", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d05:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d01:c0", "entity": "Battle of Ramla", "scope": "Third Battle of Ramla", "claim": "The third Battle of Ramla took place on 27 August 1105.", "answer": "1105", "quote": "Battle of Ramla (1105) The third Battle of Ramla (or Ramleh) took place on 27 August 1105 between the Crusader Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Fatimids of Egypt.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d02:c0", "entity": "Third Battle of Ramla", "scope": "Date of the Third Battle of Ramla", "claim": "The Third Battle of Ramla took place on 27 August 1105.", "answer": "1105", "quote": "Third Battle of Ramla Part of the Crusades Date 27 August 1105 Location Ramla 31°55′29.26″N 34°52′21.75″E Result Crusader victory Belligerents Kingdom of Jerusalem Fatimid Caliphate Burid dynasty Commanders and leaders Baldwin I of Jerusalem Sama ' al-Mulk Husayn General Sabawa", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d05", "card_id": "ramdocs-0395-c98d528f04b1:d05:c0", "entity": "Battle of Ramla", "scope": "12th-century Crusades", "claim": "The Battle of Ramla took place in 1102.", "answer": "1102", "quote": "Battle100953559 yago : Campaign100798245 yago : Conflict100958896 yago : Event100029378 yago : GroupAction101080366 yago : MilitaryAction100952963 yago : PsychologicalFeature100023100 yago : Work100575741 yago : YagoPermanentlyLocatedEntity dbo : Event dbo : MilitaryConflict yago : Undertaking100795720 yago : Venture100797878 yago : Wikicat12th-centuryCrusades umbel-rc : ConflictEvent umbel-rc : Event rdfs : comment La batalla de Ramla del 1102 fou la segona batalla entre l'exèrcit croat i l'exèrcit musulmà del Califat fatimita d'Egipte en la rodalia de Ramla .", "original_document_number": 6}], "initial_answers": ["1102", "1105"]}
